Based on my research, I have enough evidence to issue my verdict. Here are the key findings:

**Critical finding**: arXiv:2504.14633 (April 2025, "Harnessing Generative LLMs for Enhanced Financial Event Entity Extraction") does essentially the same core technical operation: fine-tunes an LLM (PEFT) to output JSON with `{text, start, end}` character indices. The proposal does not cite this paper at all.

**Qwen3.5-9B thinking mode**: Confirmed the model defaults to thinking mode by default, and critically: *"Models in thinking mode do not support structured output"*. XGrammar-2 constrained decoding requires structured output mode. This compatibility conflict is not addressed in the proposal.

**EMNLP 2026 deadline**: Confirmed as May 25, 2026. ✓

**XGrammar-2**: Confirmed released May 2026. ✓

**RelPrior numbers**: Source paper shows F1=54.80, Ign F1=54.53 on Re-DocRED test — the proposal has these values slightly off (claims 55.94 F1 / 54.80 Ign F1).

