  "verdict": "revise",
  "scores": {
    "novelty": {
      "score": 3,
      "rationale": "The core technical operation — fine-tuning an LLM to output JSON with char_start/char_end fields via CE supervision — has direct prior art in arXiv:2504.14633 (April 2025, 'Harnessing Generative LLMs for Enhanced Financial Event Entity Extraction'), which outputs {text, start, end} tuples on CCKS-2019. PAGe-IE's differentiation (complex event/relation schemas, standard IE benchmarks ACE05/Re-DocRED, faithfulness verification framework) is meaningful but the methodological leap is incremental and the omission of this citation would flag immediately in peer review."
    },
    "feasibility": {
      "score": 3,
      "rationale": "A technical incompatibility is unaddressed: Qwen3.5-9B defaults to thinking mode (generates <think>...</think> before responses), and Alibaba's documentation explicitly states thinking-mode models do not support structured output — making XGrammar-2 constrained decoding incompatible without additional configuration. Compute estimates (2–3h per H100 run, 200h total) are now realistic, but the span-alignment pipeline on Re-DocRED coreference chains and the 87–92% retention claim remain unvalidated assumptions."
    },
    "clarity": {
      "score": 4,
      "rationale": "Round 2 is substantially clearer: DPO dropped, experiments decoupled (SEM vs. F1 parity), LLM-only comparison class stated, data retention estimate provided, null-F1 fallback framed honestly. The RelPrior F1 figures are slightly off (source shows F1=54.80/Ign F1=54.53, not 55.94/54.80), which suggests the numbers were not re-verified from the primary source."
    },
    "impact": {
      "score": 3,
      "rationale": "A successful PAGe-IE would be the first training-time character-offset supervision framework validated on ACE05 and Re-DocRED, enabling provenance verification unavailable in GoLLIE/AutoRE — a useful but modest contribution. The faithfulness-via-string-check evaluation (SEM) is practical for downstream deployment, but the scientific insight (add integer fields to the output schema, train with CE) is engineering-level rather than algorithmic."
