  "issues": [
    "CRITICAL — Missing citation of direct prior art: arXiv:2504.14633 ('Harnessing Generative LLMs for Enhanced Financial Event Entity Extraction', April 2025) fine-tunes an LLM with PEFT to generate JSON with {text, start_idx, end_idx} character spans on CCKS-2019. This is structurally identical to PAGe-IE's core technical operation. Reviewers will flag this immediately. The proposal must cite this paper and differentiate: (a) 2504.14633 is limited to entity-only extraction on a single financial dataset; PAGe-IE targets entity+relation+event extraction on ACE05/Re-DocRED; (b) 2504.14633 includes no faithfulness verification framework; (c) 2504.14633 uses no constrained decoding.",
    "CRITICAL — Qwen3.5-9B thinking mode incompatibility with XGrammar-2: Qwen3.5 models run in thinking mode by default, and Alibaba's documentation explicitly states 'thinking mode models do not support structured output.' XGrammar-2 constrained decoding operates via structured output. The proposal must specify: (a) thinking mode is disabled (enable_thinking=False) during both fine-tuning and inference; (b) whether disabling thinking mode during LoRA fine-tuning affects extraction quality; or (c) an alternative base model (e.g., Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct, Mistral-7B-Instruct) that natively supports structured output without this conflict.",
    "RelPrior F1 figures are off: The source paper (arXiv:2511.08143) reports RelPrior_LLaMA3-8B at F1=54.80, Ign F1=54.53 on Re-DocRED test — not '~55.94 F1 / 54.80 Ign F1' as stated. This suggests figures were not re-verified from the primary source. Inaccurate baselines undermine reviewer trust.",
    "SEM > 90% hypothesis lacks empirical grounding: The claim that integrated position supervision achieves SEM > 90% vs. ~70–80% for post-hoc string matching is not supported by any pilot data or theoretical argument. The 70–80% post-hoc baseline is itself an estimate. This hypothesis should be presented as a testable prediction, not a claim, and a pilot experiment on a small ACE05 slice (even 200 examples) would substantially strengthen credibility.",
    "Novelty framing gap: the description does not explicitly contrast with 2504.14633, which means the paper's novelty section would be read as 'first to fine-tune LLM to output char offsets for IE' when that is factually incorrect. The differentiation must be made proactively: PAGe-IE is the first to extend training-time char-offset supervision to multi-schema IE (event arguments, relation triples) on standard NLP benchmarks with a faithfulness evaluation protocol."
