works + MoE architecture, standard LoRA recipes may need adaptation. If standard text-only IE fine-tuning is the goal, Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct or Mistral-7B-v0.3 are cleaner baselines that are text-only, well-studied for LoRA, and have established IE fine-tuning recipes. Switching the base model would avoid the thinking-mode issue and be easier to replicate.",
  "reason": "Round 2 addresses the structural flaws from Round 1 (DPO dropped, experiments decoupled, compute within budget) but introduces two new critical gaps: a direct competing paper (arXiv 2504.14633) that is uncited and shares the core technical operation, and a Qwen3.5 thinking-mode incompatibility with XGrammar-2 constrained decoding that is unaddressed."
